    "problem_statement": "Bug in lookup_users API method - parameters swapped\n\n### Problem\n\nWhen using the `lookup_users` method in the API class, the parameters for `screen_name` and `user_id` are being swapped. This causes the method to fail when trying to look up users.\n\n### Reproduction\n\nWhen trying to look up users by either screen name or user ID, the parameters are being sent to the wrong arguments:\n\n```python\n# This fails\nusers = api.lookup_users(user_id=[123456, 789012])\n\n# This also fails\nusers = api.lookup_users(screen_name=['username1', 'username2'])\n```\n\nThe issue is that when you pass a list of user IDs, they're being sent as screen names to the Twitter API, and vice versa. Additionally, the HTTP method has been changed from POST to GET, which may not be compatible with the Twitter API endpoint.\n\nThis is causing requests to fail when trying to look up users by either method."
  }
